    "alert_id": "EX2_001",
    "title": "AKI likely pre-renal, not TDF nephrotoxicity",
    "message": "Guidelines state that in patients on TDF admitted to hospital, intercurrent illnesses with dehydration or sepsis may cause renal function deterioration, in which case TDF may be continued once renal function improves. This patient has severe gastroenteritis with dehydration (BP 90/60, dry mucous membranes), a urea-to-creatinine ratio of 24:1 favouring pre-renal AKI, and urinalysis showing no protein or glucose — atypical for TDF nephrotoxicity, which typically causes proximal tubular dysfunction with proteinuria and glycosuria. Two household contacts share the same illness, supporting infectious gastroenteritis as the cause. Permanently stopping TDF is therefore not indicated by this episode. The guideline recommends checking creatinine (eGFR) in hospitalized TDF patients and continuing TDF if renal function recovers.",
    "issue_type": "plan_review",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Continue IV fluid resuscitation and treat gastroenteritis. Hold TDF temporarily only if eGFR remains severely impaired; resume TDF once renal function recovers. Do not permanently discontinue TDF for this pre-renal AKI episode.",
