      {"page_number": 40, "chunk_id": "sahcs_adult_art_2024__sahcs_adult_art_2024__p40_c2"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "alert_id": "EX2_002",
    "title": "If TDF must be stopped, use guideline-recommended substitute",
    "message": "Guidelines specify that if renal impairment develops due to TDF, the recommended alternative regimen is ABC + 3TC + DTG. If the clinician decides to discontinue TDF based on this AKI episode, the regimen should be switched to ABC + 3TC + DTG rather than simply stopping TDF without replacement, which would leave an incomplete regimen and risk virological failure in a patient currently suppressed (<50 copies/mL).",
    "issue_type": "guideline_deviation",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "If TDF is discontinued, switch to ABC + 3TC + DTG as the guideline-recommended alternative. Confirm ABC hypersensitivity risk (HLA-B*5701 if available) before initiating abacavir.",
